### Keep the type-cache stub compatible with IDetails2 notifications

**Severity:** `medium`

After `IDetails2` exposes item-change notifications, the type-cache stub also has to satisfy that event contract. This stub is only used to populate the ABI type cache, so no-op accessors preserve the intent while keeping the implementation valid.

```suggestion
    private sealed partial class SupportDetailsContent : IDetails2
    {
        public event TypedEventHandler<object, IItemsChangedEventArgs>? ItemsChanged
        {
            add { }
            remove { }
        }

        public IIconInfo? HeroImage => null;

        public string Title => string.Empty;

        public string Body => string.Empty;

        public IDetailsElement[] Metadata => [];

        public IContent[] GetContent() => [];
    }
```

### Raise ItemsChanged when toolkit details content changes

**Severity:** `high`

The details pane reads rich content through `GetContent()`, but the current toolkit setter only raises a property notification that is not part of the `IDetails2` contract. Non-toolkit implementations would have no reliable way to tell the host to refresh, and toolkit updates can be missed or duplicated. Raise `ItemsChanged` when the content array actually changes.

```suggestion
    public virtual IContent[] Content
    {
        get => _content;

        set
        {
            if (SetProperty(ref _content, value))
            {
                RaiseItemsChanged(_content.Length);
            }
        }
    }

    public virtual IContent[] GetContent() => Content;

    protected void RaiseItemsChanged(int totalItems = -1)
    {
        try
        {
            ItemsChanged?.Invoke(this, new ItemsChangedEventArgs(totalItems));
        }
        catch
        {
        }
    }
```

