### Add the ItemsChanged event state to toolkit details

**Severity:** `high`

The toolkit `Details` type becomes the default `IDetails2` implementation, so it needs the event and backing state used by the content-change notification path. Without this, a content update after the initial render has no reliable notification source.

```suggestion
using Windows.Foundation;
using Windows.Foundation.Collections;

namespace Microsoft.CommandPalette.Extensions.Toolkit;

public partial class Details : BaseObservable, IDetails2, IExtendedAttributesProvider
{
    private IContent[] _content = [];

    public event TypedEventHandler<object, IItemsChangedEventArgs>? ItemsChanged;

    public virtual IIconInfo HeroImage { get; set => SetProperty(ref field, value); } = new IconInfo();
```

