### Make rich details content refreshable through the contract

**Severity:** `high`

`GetContent()` is only sampled by the host, and `IDetails2` currently does not define how an extension tells the host that the returned content has changed. Requiring `INotifyItemsChanged` gives all implementations a contract-supported invalidation path instead of relying on a toolkit-only property name.

```suggestion
    [contract(Microsoft.CommandPalette.Extensions.ExtensionsContract, 1)]
    interface IDetails2 requires IDetails, INotifyItemsChanged {
        IContent[] GetContent();
    }
```
